Changes: retain the neutral RGB slots used by Coder, rename the exported
constants for their Theme slots, and omit terminal color quantization.
The base background uses OpenAgents' shared Coder near-black value.
The screen layout, editor, and SVG exporter are implemented in OpenAgents.

Accent values reimplement the USGC fluorescent and standard palette retained in
platform-basecoat-2025-12-19/ui/colors.rs, Git commit
94ce27a10a05e49449e8dae91a56f34e8082ab24, in the design reference archive.
OpenAgents commit 4cdd097be8479c07974685db80647cba273e7bf4 identifies that
archive as a historical design source. Only color values are used; no archived
application code is copied. Diff bands use quarter-intensity USGC red and green.

The mock Edit calls reuse the Grok diff renderer in coder-terminal and the
syntax highlighter in code-highlight, with Coder's local USGC color mapping.
Their source attribution and licenses are retained in code-highlight/NOTICE.

Transcript messages reuse the Grok Markdown layout and transcript styles in
coder-terminal, including fenced-code highlighting from code-highlight, with
the same local color mapping. Their source attribution and licenses are retained
in code-highlight/NOTICE.
